 "voice": [
  {
   "id": "vo01",
   "t": 0.03333333333333333,
   "dur": 3.033,
   "file": "vo/01.wav",
   "text": "Which holds a million Earths? They look like twins."
  },
  {
   "id": "vo02",
   "t": 4.033333333333333,
   "dur": 9.424,
   "file": "vo/02.wav",
   "text": "In your sky, the Sun and the full Moon look the same size. But one is about four hundred times wider, and four hundred times farther away."
  },
  {
   "id": "vo03",
   "t": 14.166666666666666,
   "dur": 7.567,
   "file": "vo/03.wav",
   "text": "Line Earths up across the Sun's face: a hundred and nine. Your whole world would fit inside one big sunspot."
  },
  {
   "id": "vo04",
   "t": 22.7,
   "dur": 15.172,
   "file": "vo/04.wav",
   "text": "Nearly twenty-five centuries ago, in Athens, Anaxagoras said the Sun was a fiery stone, bigger than southern Greece. Calling it a stone, not a god, got him charged with impiety. He was right. By a factor of about eight thousand."
  },
  {
   "id": "vo05",
   "t": 40.3,
   "dur": 9.439,
   "file": "vo/05.wav",
   "text": "Melt down one point three million Earths, and they'd fill it. Yet among the stars, it's ordinary. Some are more than a thousand times wider."
  },
  {
   "id": "vo06",
   "t": 53.1,
   "dur": 6.75,
   "file": "vo/06.wav",
   "text": "Astronomers even file the Sun under dwarf stars. Out there, this is what ordinary looks like."
  },
  {
   "id": "vo07",
   "t": 60.56666666666667,
   "dur": 5.713,
   "file": "vo/07.wav",
   "text": "Light time, across the Sun: about five seconds. Sun to Earth: eight minutes, twenty seconds."
  },
  {
   "id": "vo08",
   "t": 66.96666666666667,
   "dur": 5.126,
   "file": "vo/08.wav",
   "text": "Next: since this started, you've flown at least two thousand kilometers. How?"
  }
 ]
